Licences of the pixel fonts in this directory: the misc-fixed BDF files and the C
data panel/panel-pixfont-data.c that gen-pixfont.py makes of them (public domain),
and, further down, the DejaVu Sans Bold bitmaps of panel/panel-pixfont-dejavu.c
(Bitstream Vera licence, notice in DEJAVU-LICENSE).

The five BDF files are misc-fixed fonts of the X.Org font-misc-misc package, taken from
Debian's xfonts-base (trixie), converted with pcf2bdf and reduced to printable
ASCII by `gen-pixfont.py trim`. The header of each BDF file says what their
author put on them, and gen-pixfont.py refuses to use a font whose COPYRIGHT
property does not say "public domain":

    6x10.bdf    COPYRIGHT "Public domain terminal emulator font.  Share and enjoy."
    7x13B.bdf   COPYRIGHT "Public domain font.  Share and enjoy."
    7x14B.bdf   COPYRIGHT "Public domain font.  Share and enjoy."
    9x15B.bdf   COPYRIGHT "Public domain font.  Share and enjoy."
    10x20.bdf   COPYRIGHT "Public domain font.  Share and enjoy."

None of them has a COMMENT line with other terms. Public domain needs no
notice, but nothing is lost by keeping the BDF headers, which are the evidence.
Debian's copyright file for xfonts-base agrees: its entry for font-misc-misc/COPYING
is the single line "Public domain font.  Share and enjoy."

Terminus (SIL OFL 1.1) is not used: the misc-fixed fonts cover the sizes the
panel needs and have no licence text that must travel with the binary.

DejaVu Sans Bold (panel/panel-pixfont-dejavu.c, made by gen-dejavu-bitmaps.c)

The DejaVu data is different: it has a licence text that must travel with it.
panel-pixfont-dejavu.c holds 1-bit renderings of DejaVu Sans Bold at 9, 10, 11
and 12 px, made with FreeType's v35 TrueType interpreter from DejaVuSans-Bold.ttf
of Debian trixie's fonts-dejavu-core 2.37-8 (the font's own version string is
"Version 2.37"). The fonts derive from Bitstream Vera. Their copyright line is
"Copyright (c) 2003 by Bitstream, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Bitstream Vera is a
trademark of Bitstream, Inc." and "DejaVu changes are in public domain". The
copyright, trademark and permission notice is in DEJAVU-LICENSE in this
directory, the file /usr/share/doc/fonts-dejavu-core/copyright of that package
copied unchanged. The permission notice asks for the copyright and trademark
notices and the notice itself in all copies of the typefaces, so DEJAVU-LICENSE
goes with the generated data and with every copy of it; the header of the
generated file says so too. The last stanza of that file (Debian's packaging,
GPL-2+) is about the package, not the fonts.

The baked data is compiled-in bitmaps for the panel's text. It is not distributed
as a font and not under the Bitstream or Vera names; the notice allows a modified
font only under a name that has neither word. The font files themselves are not
in this repository: the generator reads the ones the package installs. This
records facts and is not legal advice.
